  "lineage": "The specifically Egyptian branch of the broader Arab tarab tradition — built on the takht ensemble (oud, qanun, ney, riq, kamancheh) plus the 20th-century Egyptian innovation of adding a large Western violin section for the Umm Kulthum / Mohammed Abdel Wahab era recordings; pre-WWII figures Sayed Darwish, Mohammed al-Qasabgi, Zakariya Ahmed, then the post-WWII Golden Age anchored by Umm Kulthum (1898-1975), Mohammed Abdel Wahab (1902-1991), Abdel Halim Hafez (1929-1977)",
